that I had nothing to do with
I can promote it shamelessly.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.860
This is a beautiful show.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:26.400
It's about the effects of incarceration

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:29.010
on the whole rest of the
family and the community.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:32.368
And it's a really laugh out loud comedy.

00:08:32.368 --> 00:08:34.830
And there's incredible choreography

00:08:34.830 --> 00:08:36.360
by Lil Buck and John Bugs.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:38.806
And there's spoken word,
which I do somehow.

00:08:38.806 --> 00:08:40.620
So it's cool.
- That's cool.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:42.633
To stretch a different muscle, right?

00:08:42.633 --> 00:08:44.940
Daveed is so funny.

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:45.780
Yes, I love him.

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:47.250
So you, you've described your character

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.110
as a hippie loud mommy.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:50.280
Do you relate to that at all?

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:51.120
Because I do.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.770
- I, when I first got the part,

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:54.720
I'm like, how am I gonna play this?

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:57.060
- You literally just said
three things that are me.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:57.893
- Oh, really?

00:08:57.893 --> 00:09:01.881
Yeah, so, you know, I put
together what she wears.

00:09:01.881 --> 00:09:05.910
I've got a wig that's got a
little more gray than I have.

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:08.700
And yeah, she's the
loud, liberal of "No one

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:11.250
in the room's gonna say
it, I'm gonna say it."

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:14.700
And then I got to work and
it was time to get dressed

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:18.090
and I took off my Birkenstocks
and put on her Birkenstocks.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.940
I took off my leg, put on her leg.

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:23.460
I rolled up my graying hair and put her,

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.833
and I was like "There's
no character here at all,

00:09:25.833 --> 00:09:26.666
it's me."

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:27.810
- [Kelly] It's just like
hanging out my skin.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.550
- It's just me.

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:30.383
- [Kelly] That's fun.

00:09:30.383 --> 00:09:31.690
- And I got hired to do it.

00:09:31.690 --> 00:09:33.570
What, what did you learn
about playing the role?

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:35.640
Did you know a lot about incarceration

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:36.570
and how it affects the family?

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:39.396
- Yeah, I mean, for
different reasons I've been,

00:09:39.396 --> 00:09:44.299
you know as a white woman
had the privilege to learn

00:09:44.299 --> 00:09:47.010
about it more slowly than
other people in our country

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:50.550
because it saturates my
community slightly less

00:09:50.550 --> 00:09:51.810
than people of color.

00:09:51.810 --> 00:09:55.950
But first of all, you know,
the prison for profit thing

00:09:55.950 --> 00:10:00.000
is, it's hard to wake up in
the morning knowing that.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.320
- I remember finding that out.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:02.850
- Yeah, no, it's, it's devastating.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:05.370
And this show, there
have been beautiful books

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:07.470
and documentaries and
movies made about that.

00:10:07.470 --> 00:10:11.280
And this show is talking about
the effects on the mothers

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:15.840
and the sons, and the
wives, and the sisters,

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:16.920
and the best friends-

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.194
- And the loved one.

00:10:18.194 --> 00:10:20.460
- You know, the concentric
circle of, of suffering

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:22.955
That this system causes and somehow it's-

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:24.300
- You don't think about it.

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.250
- No, if you have the privilege
not to think about it.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.743
- [Kelly] Unless it's
impacting you, yeah, wow.

